        <p>MEIE CORPORATION OF WARRINGTON is prepered to receive lease, either at six months notice or for a term of years.—Application to be made to the BOROUGH TRIASURZR, Municipal Ofgoes, Warrington. COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Pewee for the COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER will be held Ilat the COURT-HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, in and for the raid County, on MONDAY, the 3rd day of APRIL NEXT, et 4 Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when the Grand Jury will be empennelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Altrincham,Bucklow,Dukintield, Middlewich, Sandbach, Congleton, Northwich, Prem. bury and Stockport, forming the Knutaford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Divisions, will take place at such Sessions. The Greed and Petty Juries for the Knotsford District most be is attendance at the COURT HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 3rd day of APRIL NEXT, at Eleven o'clock lathe Forenoon. THE COURT will be Adjourned to the CASTLE OP CHESTER on WEDNESDAY, the sth day of APRIL NEXT,at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. rim hear in of all Appeals arising within the Petty SessionM Divisions of Broxton, Chester Castle, Dareabary, Eddisbury, Nantwich, Runcorn, Winaford, and Wirral, • forming the Cheater District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-mentioned Divisions will take place at each Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Cheater District most • be in attendance at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, at the opening of the Court on WEDNESDAY, the sth • day of APRIL NEXT, at Eleven o'clock in the • Forenoon.</p>
        <p>REGINALD POSTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County Palatine of Cheater.</p>
        <p>Chester, 21st March, 1911.</p>
        <p>/101-NTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— 1.../ The Sanitary Works Committee are prepared to receive Tenders for the supply of about 15 tons per week of good Firing Slack,to be delivered at Longford Depot In such quantities as may be required during sin months, commencing 13th April, 1911. The contractor whose tender is accepted will be required to observe the recognised customs and addl. tiona as to rate of wages and working hours p 'ling within the distriot. Tenders, securely fastened, most be addressed, "Th. Chairman, Sanitary Work. Committee, Town Hall, ' Warrington," endorsed "Tender for Slack," and delivered not later than Tueeday, 4th April, 1911. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. It. W Longford Depot, Warrington. ~d March, 1911.</p>
        <p>R. WILSON, ida.ger.</p>
        <p>U N CORN UN IO N.—CONTRACTS for PROVISIONS and SUPPLIES forth. Half-year ending September Met, 1911. The Guardians of the Poor of the Runcorn Union are desirouo of receiving TENDERS from parties willing to Contract for the supply of Good Beef, to consist of vein pieces intact and Flat Rib. with bone one round weekly not to exceed 2Mbs., and 4511 m. per week of the Best Butcher's Meat, including Teel, lamb and pork (in mason) for the Officer. ; Side' of Mutton (all meat to be English killed); Bread, Orooeriee, Drapery, Clothing, Boots, Boot Repairing, Potatoes, Straw, Drywiltery, Brushes and Mats. Wines, Spirits, Coal, Slack,Coke, Deal Coffins, Horse Hire (for tuners!. end muting), Milk (for 12 months), Tobacco, and Snuff. Earthenware, Hardware, Oils and Colours. Tenders are also invited from Tradesmen for the service. per hour of Journeymen and Apprentices of the following trades .—Plumber, Joiner, Whiteemitb, and Bricklayer. Parties tendering for the supply of the above- mentioned Goods will be required to deliver the same at the Workhouse, free of cost to the Guardians, how and when required. Tenders to he accompanied with samples (except Drapery Goods and Clothing) as far as procurable. The Guardians do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any Tender. Pomo* desirous of tendering must apply by letter to my office, in Runcorn, for a printed Form of Tender (and none other can be entertained), where a Schedule of the various articles required and further particulars</p>
        <p>may he obtained. Sealed Tenders, addressed to the Guardians, to be forwarded to the Clerk's Office, Runcorn, on or before Monday, the 27th day of March, 1911, endorsed Tender for The Tenders will be opened and considered at a Meeting of the Guardians to be held in the Board-room, Dotter, on the 28th ,ay of March, 1911, at I p.m. Parties whose tenders are acoepted must enter into a written contract and be prepared to eater into a Bond, with two Sureties, if required by the Guardians. . .</p>
        <p>By order of the Board, OkO. F. ASHTON, Clerk to the Guardians.</p>
        <p>Runcorn, 11th Much, 1911.</p>
