        <p>D AND MODERN RESEARCH. ation continues to unfold to us its e peat. One of the most striking was ofessor Piochea at a meeting at tha to on Monday evening. Ile told of • , at has been found and translated by I Hilprecbt. It was three and three- nog by two and three-eightlminches in greatest thickness seven-eighths of are g to Professor Hilprecht and other loglsts it belong. to the period between c. Thus it is four thousarwl years old, ddition to the many referermes to • Ito ancient Scripture.. According to echt's rendering, the writiows contain I will loosen the confines of heaven II make • flood. •ed it will sweep away or." Then followed Instructions to hip," and that "every beast ot the field • heavens should be brought therein." Dom between this record and the story Atk im too clam to nape mtleatiom.—</p>
