owners —large end small—ln this country. la spite of what had been mid about Wife landowners in London, they found that in that city there weru 34,600 land owners., the largest of whore were the Ct.., the Eccleeiastioal Commiasioners the Londen County Council and the City Corporation who rutted 19 square miles out of 113. In all limo mem he hail mentioned the land virtu- ally belonged to the people, because lie took it that the Crown Janda bad been taken over and the renta went to pay the talary of the monarch, while in the cue of the Emlesinetical Cumnioners the rento from their property went to the upkeep of churche, which were for the people. lo London there were 183 large landowners who owned a third of a slum mile each, and 31,113 owners who bad about no acre each. The only method of thrift that appealed to the workingman mum invest- ment in house property nod be was assured that he would not have to pay increment val. duty. Ile (the speaker) bad it on the authority of the eecretary of a large property asseciation in Yorkshire that up to Ih.ceniter ledh, 7,7.0 provisional valuations bed Men .• . .</p>
        <p>. - received by the'rnernhere, that 700 of them were 30 per eent.helow the original coat,and 5000 f them were below the actual mortgages. The mink was that those people, representing be thrifty workingmen of Leeds, were rewei•ing notice from the mortgegee• to cell In the "</p>
        <p>ulna/rites, and he was told that the total mortgegat railed in up to date rnpresooted irroo,ooo. That,he orrn- , tended, was • hkrdship inflicted upon Lbw thrifty work- ' ingot., In many cases tbe taxes were nut only ioequilable lot imrsural.</p>
        <p>" wyA:r. IS .7111, LAn.UNION CREATED</p>
        <p>....,.. ... ..... ~...... ...........—......—... continued Mr. Vince. " Weald created for the RAMO mason that the Licensed Trade Defence Association I...created. The moment they came within the area of Demi°it they bad to organize themselves in golf- defekce. We have taken the mune steps. and has now ! become • taxable quantity, end therefore those who !poseese land or interest in land—and you cannot build , hodsera in the air : if you own property you ono land— , rt 'dieing it is time,they got together and orgatrised. 1 ir idual effort will not open the doors of the Treasury your complaint., but organized effort will. The licy of the Union I. to work etrentionely for the endment,certainly, and we hope for the final striking it of the land taxon. Bid half • loaf is better t n none, and therefore we want to sort for amenilmeet first. . . . . We do tot know a t these texts are going to bring fotth. We argon that the Goverment have not gone through this i</p>
