        <p>The toast was cordially drunk and Bro. DD. It. Attire: in replying said that they ought to be proud of the Order. They were certainly not the oldest Order, bet ' they were amcngst the aix largeat. Deprecating tontine club the speaker rid that it wee bad policy for people to be connected with them, juiet for the mere di•idiog up et Christmas. (Orr, hear.) Ile ' wintered satisfaction owing to the ermine of the Chancellor of the Exchequer to subsidise Friendly Societiee. The King William IV. lodge bad always been zealous workers and he hoped that during the year of nice of Bro. Rushton that tteir members would rill increase greatly. (Applause.)</p>
