        <p>Cutimint soap and ointment do en much for poor complexions, red, rough hands, and dry, thin and falling hair, and cost no little that it is 'lmmo criminal not to use them. Think of tbe miffering entailed by neglected akin troubles—mental Mesa., of disfiguration —physiral because of pain. Think a the pleasure of a clear nkin, soft white hands and good hair. These blessing. Sr. often only • matter of • little thoughtful timely care, vir...—warns baths with Cutiettra amp, *misted when necessary by gentle anointing, with Cotiritra ointnwnt. Fall iiirectiona for the care of the akin, wall.. hair and lisnds, are given in the !steel 3:!-Inge Courant book SOpt poet free on application, by the Potter Drug 4 chem. Corp., 27, Cbarterbouse Sy., London, EC.</p>
