        <head>EXAMINER. RDAY. MARCH 25 199.</head>
        <p>EXAMINER. RDAY. MARCH 25 199.</p>
        <p>But for rumours and S IN "incidents," the pro- jSE. ceedings of the House</p>
        <p>of Commons would be along rather wearily just now. ways the possibility that some e going about the Lobby, or den storm may have arisen in . favourite rumour just now is I g else is to be substituted for t Bill. This is absurd on the I iless it be assumed that the I he Parliament Bill be con- the necessity of passing that Runciman " incident " was Wednesday, contrary to some Consideration of the facts has it appear that the PRESIDENT ID OF EDUCATION had some ag his temper, though it would isable for him to have kept it</p>
        <p>two or three more or less lively ng the earlier portion of</p>
