        <p>Ths Rev. AJ. Waldrop, •itier of Brixton. Londoe, addreased large gatherings of women and men in the . afternoon and evening respectively at the Parieh Church, yeaterday. In tine ;afternoon he spoke on the , Power of Personality... and in the ermine his subject wee "Th. Bible Is it true?" He dealt first with the modern criticism of the Bible and he said that that bad caused an to take what be called • more rational view of the Bible. Before modern criticism Christiana had to apologise for certain thing. atd defend them, whereee now they bad to explain them from the standard of comparative religious study. Referring to the new paycholoey an expounded by Sir Oliver Lodge he mid that it gave ao interpretion of supernatural elemente and helped in the *elution of the mental licaaltaea of people In regard to religion. The preacher contended that the Bible ass inapi red and that if it had Dot been so it would not have had such a remarkable influence on national aid individual life, on social prottrws, riraoation, literat•tre, art, mimic and economics. e•ditiniting. he aid that a system of philomphy must he a system or mein principles—not of detail—and this was what the New Teataromtoootained. Tb. Old Testament Morae were more or less negative —" Treepassera will be prosecuted "—and the New Testament was positive—" Blessed are the merciful." Though it bad been said thet before the Chrietian religion there were sauterne of advanced morals, yet uatil the advent of Christ pogo were able to meterialise thaw principles. The fact Wet Christ carried out His moral precepts Ind a greeter leffueeme over the world thee any Other ey.terti.</p>
