        <p>Roberts and H. Thornton. As A tilt ISO Crirrom sm.—John Mulligan, 39, Tilley- street, Warrington, wan charged with using abusive langunge in Mersey•street and assaulting a publican named Hanley.—Mr. Hanley stated thrit prisoner came into bin house on Saturday end asked for a pint of beer. Ile nerved him, and noon afterwards prisoner com- menced to quarrel with the other customers. Witness gave him his 23d. back and risked him to go, and prisoner commenced to nrgue Raying " Von can't pist me out," end need abußive language. On witness getting ...o/il of him klullignn "butted" him in the face. The Prisoner : I ani very sorry. It was quite accidental, if I did hit him.—The Chief Constable tinted that Mulligan had been up 23 times previously. It is not fair," he added, "when a landlord is endeavouring to carry on his house in a respectable manner for men to make disturbance. like this."—The Prisoner : I will never take another dro" of drink as long as I lire, I will be tee-total.—The Chairman: On that undertnking you will fined On, including costa. It would have been more if you had not made that procaine.</p>
