        <p>In the Spring most people complain of a decline in health. Some have a deprenned and tired-out feeling which sleep does not dispel; others suffer from stomach and digestive weakness. Again many endure painful attacks of Nruralgia, also skin disorders. This general outbreak of minor ailments is a clear indication that the blood is in an impure condition ; it means that the body needs help in the form of Good New Blood, that will purify the system and give strength to the nerves. At this time of the year, Dr. Williams' Pink Pills are especially necessary for ailing ones of both snare because they do create Rich Blood—the greatest need in Spring—and it is this New Blood that clears the skin, dispels Rheumatism, and nerve pains, and makes weak, woin-out men and women fresh and fit for work. Ilere are two instances in proof.</p>
