        <p>Mr. Bert Adams, of 130, Richmond Park Road, Kingaton-on-Than3es : "In the spring of last year I began to feel out of sorts. My appetite failed and I felt too unwell to give proper attention to my work. Tonics and aperients were tried, but my blood became more impoverished ; then Eczema developed. Illy hands, arms, legs and back were badly attacked. A doctor gave me medicine but the terrible itching increased and I was compelled to remain in bed. " Then I read in the newspapers of a case of Eczema which bad been cured by Dr. Williitms' Pink Pills. So a supply of these Pills was sent for, and after taking the Pills for some time the Eczema became leFs irritating. In time the New Good Blood given me by Dr. William.' Pink Pills drove all traces of the Eczema from my system. My skin resumed its former healthy appearance, and soon I was fit and well." An interewing and instructive booklet, " Diseases of the blood," will be sent post free to applicants. Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People have cared Skin Disorders, Eczema, Rheumatism, Indigestion, Neuralgia,Anremia,Debility,Sciatica,NervemeDisorelers dreaded by men, and the ills of women. Of dealers, or direct from Dr. Williams' Medicine Co., 46, Holborn Viaduct,Londoo,post free 2s. 9d. one boz,or 13s. 9d. for sir. Accept only the genuine Dr. Williams' Pink Pills.</p>
