      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-03-25_WidnesExaminer_art0132" n="art0132">
        <head>LABOUR RE QUIREMENTS FOR BRITISII COLUMBIA.</head>
        <p>LABOUR RE QUIREMENTS FOR BRITISII COLUMBIA.</p>
        <p>The labour requiremeots for British Columbia are likely to to very great this year. At the same time, any indiecrimlnate rush of person. to that part and especially to the cities, regardless of the local con- ditions in to be deprecated, an it can only rod in hard- ship an'd disappointment. In all probability the demand for skilled tradesmen in Vancouver will be large, but congestion may easily occur, and these who go out in excess of the requirements mum be prepared to take alternative employment elsewhere on railway conetruc- lion worke, etc., which will require n vast army of me.. This fact, nay. Mr. .1. Brace Walker, the Caoadian Commiseioner of Immigration, Winnipeg, makes the prospect for the unskilled Inbourer on railway work very bright. In anticipation of the nab to British Columbia, end particularly to Vancouver, of unskilled labour unaccustomed to manual work. Mr. Walker desires that these persons should be warned against math a mum. There in no demand for unskilled labour of a clerical character in the province of Britieb Columbia. Persons affected by the.. conditions are strongly advised to take their tickets in the first place no further than Winnipeg; and to arrange to accept employment in the prairie provinces, where the demand for unskilled labour on forms is likely to be fat is enema of the supply.</p>
      </div>
