        <p>" Ever since I wires little girl, thirty years ago. I had suffered tortures from eczema in one of its worvt forms. The disease rtine in my family. and ruins of • scaly and in at disfiguring kind. lie eczema formed in round rings, and then scales all over my face and limbs. I have been smothered from head to foot. I was born in Leamington, which is famous for its sulphur baths and pump waters, and osie wall , Mink that after taking the treatment there regulzrly sal did, the disease would have lug ago have been cured, but it was not. I attended the --- Hospital for sears and years, an you will seal gave its fair trial. Everyone fn the town knew of my case. When I was • girl, I lived f r • shut time at Chepeltown, Leeds, and I wan treated at a hospital there, but with- out receiving any benefit. My fern was disfigured very badly. A doctor told me that I should hover get rid of it. I "Tent pounds in metre' i,ilte, •nd I attended several hospitals, but nothing did me any good.. . .</p>
