        <p>The Bible is Ineuti folly bound in porple velvet with silver mount.. Inside tbe cover is printed this inscription : • '</p>
        <p>Presented to his Pajesty King Georg* Ve by the members of the deputation remised by his klaprety on the occasion of the celebration of the tercentenary of lb. Autborieed Version of the Englis'i !tittle. The address, which accompanied the Bible, contained the following striking partages The growth and strength of the Empire owe much to the English Bill. It has sweetened home life ; it has tot etaudard of pure speech ;it hen permeated liters- , tore sad art ; it has helped to remove social wrongs and to ameliorate conditions of labour; it has modified , the laws of the realm and :Japed the national character and it has fostered international comity and goodwill laming. MP.</p>
        <p>-I.ll7l;e—c-o.une of his nply to the iddrees, lii. Majnay said :</p>
        <p>It IS my confident hope, mnifirmed by the widespread inteiest your movement lois aroused, that my rutijecis may never cease to cberish their noble Inheritance in the English Bible, which in a secular event la the filet of national treasure, and is, an you truly fray, in its spiritual significance " the most valuable thing that this world affords:.</p>
