        <p>LORDS AS UNFAIR REFEREES.</p>
        <p>LABOURER CHARGED WITH ARSON. At St. flume. Police Court on Wedne•Cay, George Wolfe, a middle-aged farm labourer, wee charged in custody with arson, by setting tire to stern. Sergeant Fidliog said that the fire was discovered by Police-constable Cunliffe, who was going his rounds. j He wee travelling the Rainford-road, when he noticed: smoke and flames isauiug from the barn at the farm of Mrs. Ann Hurst. He immediately went on the farm, and saw the prisoner running from the direction in which the fire was. Ile knew bun, and spoke to him, , end then set to work to arouse the inmates of the farm- house which closely adjoined the farm. When the brigade had extinguished the fire, the constable apprehended Wolfe, who at first said that he</p>
