        <p>the Eucharist as be dose as "Made up of , EIIMILY and an Heavenly," if he had belie Would Theodoret, tn. 123, eay "The Sarni depart from their proper nature after the Cr_ for they remain in their farmer substance air, I and form," if he had so believed' Would, ... Pope Gelasins Bishop of Rome, 492. say ..io he id "Mt Secrentents *kick we receive are the i, reality of the Bode and 'Mood of Christ, ether ire comes to pasal,th.that we by them are made pa ,ak of the Divine Nature and that never thelessthe a tat or nature cf the Bread and Wine does not</p>
